---
description: Ban TypeScript type-escaping hacks (non-null !, as any, ts-ignore)
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: true
---

# No TypeScript escaping

Do not silence the typechecker. Prefer correct types over assertions.

## Banned

- Definite assignment / non-null assertions: `prop!: Type`, `value!`, `foo!.bar`
- `as any`, `as unknown as T` used only to bypass checking
- `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-nocheck` in hand-written code
- `@ts-expect-error` without a one-line justification comment on the same or next line

## Allowed alternatives

- TypeORM / class-validator class fields: use `declare prop: Type` (runtime filled by framework)
- Late init (e.g. Nest `onModuleInit`): `T | undefined` + a private getter that throws if missing
- Cross-realm bridges (Puppeteer ↔ page): ambient `declare global` typings, not `as any`
- Generated files (e.g. `routeTree.gen.ts`): leave alone; keep excluded from lint

## Examples

```ts
// BAD
id!: string;
(window as any).__stopRecording = fn;
private worker!: Worker;

// GOOD
declare id: string;
window.__stopRecording = fn;
private worker: Worker | undefined;
private requireWorker(): Worker {
  if (!this.worker) throw new Error('worker not initialized');
  return this.worker;
}
```
